I want to go to the other side.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:40.060
Birk might be somewhere beyond all this rubble!

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:44.400
With her fever gone, Ronja was back to her old self again.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:51.950
Throughout the snowstorm, Ronja worked to clear the stones blocking the passage,

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.080
Hoping for a chance to see Birk again.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.220
Then one day...

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:05.380
A Whistle in the Basement

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:05.380
A Whistle in the Basement

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.410
Ronja?

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.450
Birk?

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:22.750
Birk? Is that really you?

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.340
Is it true that you want to be my brother?

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.640
My sister.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.830
It's great to hear your voice...

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.650
But I'd really like to see your face too.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:50.230
Are your eyes still black as ever?

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.030
Come and see for yourself!

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:00.990
Shh.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.100
Tomorrow.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.290
I've searched everywhere!

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:50.460
What in the name of all the wild harpies

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:55.050
have you been doing down here?

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:02.470
I can't just shovel snow <i>all</i> the time.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:06.540
Come on, I want to get out of here.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:16.240
True, you can't just shovel snow day in and day out.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.280
It's too cold down here though.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.950
You can play dice all night and day, though.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.040
Don't you think?

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:38.260
Yes I do! Especially now, right?

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:02.300
It's ready.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.040
Uh-huh.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:04.220
I wonder why Dad didn't think to use the
 underground passage to get at Borka's robbers?

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.190
But, I'm glad...

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:21.440
They should be allowed to stay in their part of the castle.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.990
For Birk's sake.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:29.940
Tomorrow.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:31.450
When tomorrow comes...

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:58.910
This needs to be done at least once a week.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:05.740
Otherwise, people will laugh at you and say things like, "The Mattis robber girl is infested with lice!"

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.020
You too, Mattis!

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.720
Ow-ow-ow...

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:37.390
Ow-ow-ow...

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.190
Ow-ow-ow...

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:43.440
Ow-ow-ow!

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:57.000
Twelve matted, lousy robbers are enough!

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.570
But at this rate, all of my hair will be gone!

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:07.880
I intend to comb the chief, dead or alive,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:14.820
for as long as I can manage to lift a lice comb!

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.770
Give me a break!

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:21.940
It's stopped snowing completely.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.510
It hasn't been sunny like this in forever.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.110
That makes me hungry, too!

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:32.490
Everyone, go outside and work for a bit.

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:34.990
Huh? This early in the morning?

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.160
You want us to work before breakfast?

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:41.500
Finish your work before it starts snowing again.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:42.380
Huh?

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:53.050
Last night I was thinking up a new way to get rid of Borka's robbers, I hardly slept at all.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:59.350
You're such a great bandit chief, you can even think while you snore!

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.350
Keep talking, gramps.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:05.480
This time you'll kneel before me in admiration.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.610
But, I can't talk about it here.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.950
It would take a while to explain.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.230
Oh...

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:22.580
Then let's go discuss it in my room.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:27.000
I was hoping you'd say that.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.220
Why are you guys all standing around like dimwits?!

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.390
Y-Yeah.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:16.850
I can eat just as well underground.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:23.520
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:23.520
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:02.520
Birk.

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:08.360
Birk!

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:14.320
Birk?

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:30.880
I've been waiting a long time.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:34.470
And so have I!

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:39.930
I've been waiting ever since I got away from the rumphobs!

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:48.690
Sure enough, you've still got those same black eyes.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.700
But you've gotten a bit paler.

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.830
What have you been doing with yourself?

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.410
Nothing.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.750
I just haven't been eating much.

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:13.710
Even so, I've had more than anyone else in Borka's Keep.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:17.940
Do you mean that you haven't had any food?

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:20.340
You don't have enough to eat?

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.810
Eat?

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:26.390
None of us has had enough to eat for a long time.

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:32.860
If spring doesn't come soon, we'll all be done for.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.360
Just like you wanted.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.950
You remember, right?

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:46.750
That was before. I didn't have a brother then.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.460
Things are different now!

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.710
Now, I have a brother!

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:08.390
If you're hungry, eat up!

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:02.850
Shouldn't you have kept this for yourself?

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.660
I'm not starving.

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:07.950
Besides...

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.790
There's more at home.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.810
Why is everyone on your side hungry?

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:46.070
We're poor robbers for the time being, you see.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:53.160
We're reaching the end of our food stocks.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:10.890
We had goats, and sheep too, before we came here.

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:13.390
Now we have nothing but our horses.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:18.860
We stabled them for the winter with a farmer, down beyond Borka's forest.

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.610
Thank goodness we did,

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:26.860
otherwise we would have eaten them too.

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:32.370
Yeah, we've really been having a terrible winter.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:44.920
Poor robbers—that's what we are.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:51.930
You've noticed how I reek of dirt and poverty.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.770
We've scarcely any water either.

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:11.820
We weren't able to draw enough from the stream,

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.660
so now we've resorted to melting snow.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:22.540
For even a small amount of water we need to burn what little wood we have,

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:25.550
and it takes a really long time.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:34.430
So that's why I smell like a dirty robber.

00:17:35.310 --> 00:17:38.980
Our robbers smell the same.

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:51.070
<i>My brother is handsome...</i>

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:58.750
Even if you're poor, lousy, and dirty,

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:01.540
that doesn't matter!

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:06.210
But I don't want you to go hungry!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:10.220
How did you know that I was lousy?

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:17.720
Yeah, I certainly am.

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:22.690
But I'd rather be lousy than hungry.

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:24.730
That's for sure.

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:29.280
Being hungry is terrible.

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:36.870
I probably should have saved a bit of bread for my mother, Undis.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:40.500
I can get some more!

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:42.370
You can't!

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:49.550
I can't take bread home to my mother without telling her where I got it.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:54.300
And my father would be beside himself with fury if he found out about this.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:59.060
Even more so, if he knew that I'd become your brother.

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:07.570
Why on earth does everything have to be so complicated?

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:13.410
We can never meet except in secret.

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:19.540
That's true, but I hate doing things in secret.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:21.500
Me too!

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.250
There's nothing I hate more

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:29.880
than old saltfish and long winters.

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:35.430
But it's ridiculous that we have to keep this secret, I hate it just as much!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:41.850
But you'll do it all the same?

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.440
For my sake.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:46.190
Yup.

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:50.440
It'll be easier in spring, we could meet in the woods then.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.280
Instead of this ice cold pit of a cellar.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.910
I think I should go now...

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:07.670
Before I freeze to death.

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:25.020
Will you come back tomorrow?

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:29.110
To your lousy brother?

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:32.280
Yeah.

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.910
Ronja kept her promise.

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:49.040
Early every morning, as long as the winter lasted,

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:52.840
she met Birk down in the cellar vaults and kept him alive.

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:35.300
Here.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:41.050
And this is for your mother.

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:51.560
I feel as if I were stealing from you.

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:57.530
Aren't I a robber's daughter?

00:21:57.530 --> 00:22:03.410
A robber takes without asking or getting permission.

00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:06.450
Even I've learned at least that much.

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:14.590
In the first place, much of this was already stolen from rich merchants traveling through the woods.

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.550
Except that bread, my mother baked that!

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:26.600
I'm just doing what I was taught.

00:22:26.600 --> 00:22:29.100
So quit worrying and just eat up.

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:30.650
Uh-huh.

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:58.070
Ronja would be in deep trouble if Mattis ever found out.

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:02.430
So it's come to this—helping Borka robbers...

